<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sankuru River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sankuru is a river of the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-republic-of-the-congo">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a> and the main tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kasai">Kasai</a>, which it joins after a course of about 1,200 kilometres. Together with the Kasai it bounded the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quba">Kuba</a> kingdom, and it gives its name to Sankuru province.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sankuru-river.jpg" alt="Sankuru River" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sankuru_River_entering_Kasai_River_NASA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
